# /etc/vector/conf.d — manual Vector drop-ins
#
# Any *.yaml here is merged ON TOP of /etc/vector/vector.yaml by the vector
# service (vector multi-config: later files win). This is the supported way
# to add sinks (e.g. a remote log endpoint) WITHOUT touching the package-
# managed base config.
#
# Rules:
#   - component IDs must not collide with the base config (sources: syslog,
#     internal_logs, dinit_services, incus_logs, user_session_logs; sinks:
#     messages, auth_log, daemon_log, kernel_log, sudo_log, firewalld_log,
#     user_session_log)
#   - reference the sources above as inputs; never re-declare them
#   - validate before restarting: vector validate --skip-healthchecks
# The session-runtime source (user_session_logs) tails /run/user/*/*.log —
# a session tool writing $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/<name>.log is picked up
# automatically; ship it with a drop-in sink when needed.
